RPCS3 with a native RTX Remix render backend
============================================

This build submits PlayStation 3 geometry to the RTX Remix runtime through the
Remix API, so a PS3 title is path traced rather than rasterised. It is a research
build, not a product. Read the "What works" section before filing anything.

Source and full documentation:
  https://github.com/BRAGme/rpcs3-rtx


TWO THINGS ARE NOT IN THIS ZIP AND IT WILL NOT RUN WITHOUT THEM
---------------------------------------------------------------

1. THE REMIX PLUS RUNTIME.

   This backend does NOT work with the stock NVIDIA RTX Remix runtime. Stock is
   on the 0.6.x API line; this build needs the Remix Plus fork, which reserves
   REMIXAPI_VERSION_MINOR = 1000. The version handshake rejects stock outright.

   Get it here:
     https://github.com/RemixProjGroup/dxvk-remix   (maintainer: Kim2091)
     Release tag: remix-plus-1.5.1
     Asset:       Remix_Plus_v1.5.1_x64_games_release.zip

   Unzip it into a subfolder called  remix\  next to rpcs3.exe:

     rpcs3.exe
     remix\d3d9.dll
     remix\...

   DO NOT put d3d9.dll directly beside rpcs3.exe. Anything else in the process
   that resolves that name would pick it up. The subfolder is mandatory, not a
   convention. If you keep the runtime elsewhere, set RPCS3_REMIX_DLL to the
   full path of its d3d9.dll instead.

   It is not bundled here because that folder contains third-party redistributables
   (nvngx_dlss*.dll, cudart64_13.dll, GFSDK_Aftermath, libxess.dll,
   amd_fidelityfx_vk.dll) with their own terms, inside someone else's fork build.
   Get it from the people who made it.

2. PS3 FIRMWARE. Same as stock RPCS3 -- install it yourself from a PS3UPDAT.PUP
   you own. No firmware, games or keys are included or ever will be.


ENABLING THE BACKEND
--------------------

  Settings -> GPU -> Renderer -> RTX Remix

There is also a Settings -> RTX Remix tab for the backend's own knobs. Every knob
also has an RPCS3_REMIX_* environment variable, which always wins over the GUI.
The full table is in docs/remix/KNOBS.md in the repository.

Per-title configs for a few titles ship in config\custom_configs\ and apply
automatically when you run those titles.


WHAT WORKS, AND WHAT DOES NOT
-----------------------------

Three titles have been run. They are not equally exercised, so what each one
actually establishes is listed rather than a "works / doesn't" verdict.

  Resistance 2 (NPEA00431)  -- the primary development title, and where nearly
    every measurement comes from: camera recovery from vertex-program ucode,
    world transforms, texcoords and albedo, both skinning families, per-draw
    blend state, sky classification, 2D UI compositing.

  Haze (BLUS30094)          -- a second, structurally different engine. It skins
    on the SPU, so vertices reach RSX already animated, and it has no 'layered'
    vertex programs at all. Matching ADD's src2 constant here recovered 71% of
    world transforms that had been drawing at identity. This title is the
    evidence the ucode approach is not fitted to one game.

  Minecraft: PS3 Edition (NPUB31419) -- camera parity, quantised chunk meshes,
    and the texture-cache design. Texture identity is descriptor-only rather
    than content-sampled because of a measurement here: content-rehashing
    dragged mesh creation from 5,881 creates / 887 live to 188,427 / 31,793
    over 9,120 frames, because the albedo hash folds into the mesh key.

Not working / known bad:
  - A subset of draws still lands at runaway positions and reads as white shards.
  - Frame rate swings hard with view complexity: ~55 fps in a bounded interior,
    ~12 fps on a wide outdoor draw list.
  - Haze's shadow-receiving draws land untextured. They bind a 2048x2048 DEPTH16
    shadow map on the lowest referenced texture unit and the ucode names no
    albedo unit, so 55,360 draws in one capture reached Remix with no texture.
    Commit 0d3d3517 walks past that refusal and IS in this build, but it is
    build-verified and NOT run-verified. RPCS3_REMIX_RETRYUNSUP=0 reverts it.
  - Only these three titles have ever been run. Anything not named above is
    untested, which is not the same as broken.
  - Keyboard input is dead under Remix unless rtx.useNewGuiInputMethod = False
    is set in rtx.conf. Controllers are unaffected.

The repository README is honest about the rest and cites the measurements.


BUILD PROVENANCE
----------------

  rpcs3.exe built from  BRAGme/rpcs3-rtx  branch remix-backend, commit @GIT_SHORT@,
  reporting @GIT_REV@.
  Everything here is buildable from that commit; see BUILDING.md in the repo,
  and the "Known traps on Windows" section of the README, which will save you
  the four failures we hit.

RPCS3 is GPL-2.0. This is a modified fork; the complete corresponding source is
the repository linked at the top.
